# Upstream snapshot — fetched, never committed (ADR-0004). data/derived/ IS
# committed (ADR-0042, supersedes ADR-0028) — do not add it here.
data/upstream/

# The graph, split by what it restates (ADR-0060).
#
# `graph/approved.ttl` and `graph/inferred.ttl` ARE committed: they are this
# repo's own work, they are small enough to read, and a diff of approved.ttl is
# a diff of what a reviewer changed.
#
# `graph/source.ttl` and `graph/dataset.nq` are not. They restate the pinned
# upstream corpus, and committing 6.5MB of it here is `data/upstream/` by
# another route — the thing ADR-0004 exists to prevent. Both rebuild in one
# command: `tmk-fetch-upstream && tmk-graph --write --rules`.
graph/source.ttl
graph/dataset.nq

# The dashboard's copies of the generated reports.
#
# `site/data/*.json` IS committed — it is what the site reads, and a diff of it
# is a diff of what the published page now says. These four are different: they
# are byte copies of files already committed under `data/derived/reports/`, put
# beside the site so a block can fetch them. Committing them would put the same
# text in the history twice. `tmk-dashboard --write` recreates them.
site/data/reports/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Models, embeddings, indexes — rebuildable, often large
*.faiss
*.npy
*.pt
.cache/

